{"query": "Job 38:4\u20137; Psalm 33:6", "canonical": "Job 38:4\u20137; Psalm 33:6", "parsed": [[18038004, 18038007], [19033006, 19033006]], "passage_meta": [{"canonical": "Job 38:4\u20137", "chapter_start": [18038001, 18038041], "chapter_end": [18038001, 18038041], "prev_verse": 18038003, "next_verse": 18038008, "prev_chapter": [18037001, 18037024], "next_chapter": [18039001, 18039030]}, {"canonical": "Psalm 33:6", "chapter_start": [19033001, 19033022], "chapter_end": [19033001, 19033022], "prev_verse": 19033005, "next_verse": 19033007, "prev_chapter": [19032001, 19032011], "next_chapter": [19034001, 19034022]}], "passages": ["<h2 class=\"extra_text\">Job 38:4\u20137</h2>\n<p class=\"block-indent\"><span class=\"begin-line-group\"></span>\n<span id=\"p18038004_01-1\" class=\"line\"><b class=\"verse-num inline\" id=\"v18038004-1\">4&nbsp;</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;\u201cWhere were you when I laid the foundation of the earth?</span><br /><span id=\"p18038004_01-1\" class=\"indent line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tell me, if you have understanding.</span><br /><span id=\"p18038005_01-1\" class=\"line\"><b class=\"verse-num inline\" id=\"v18038005-1\">5&nbsp;</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;Who determined its measurements\u2014surely you know!</span><br /><span id=\"p18038005_01-1\" class=\"indent line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Or who stretched the line upon it?</span><br /><span id=\"p18038006_01-1\" class=\"line\"><b class=\"verse-num inline\" id=\"v18038006-1\">6&nbsp;</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;On what were its bases sunk,</span><br /><span id=\"p18038006_01-1\" class=\"indent line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;or who laid its cornerstone,</span><br /><span id=\"p18038007_01-1\" class=\"line\"><b class=\"verse-num inline\" id=\"v18038007-1\">7&nbsp;</b>&nbsp;&nbsp;when the morning stars sang together</span><br /><span id=\"p18038007_01-1\" class=\"indent line\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;and all the sons of God shouted for joy?</span><br /></p><span class=\"end-line-group\"></span>\n<p>(<a href=\"http://www.esv.o